※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 8501 IMPL_BACKEND_UNSUPPORTED

※ A function that answers with a character is not one the back ends generate
※ yet: a return names the kinds of value it knows how to hand back, and a
※ character is not among them.  The compiler says so rather than guessing
※ which register the answer goes in.

@[visible]
fn same(c: char) → char:
    c

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    0u6
